> Clara Santo – Future Generation International Missions Inc.
Clara was[ brought to] another orphanage before she came to Faith House. Little is known about Clara’s past prior to being[ placed] at the other orphanage. Social Services eventually closed down the orphanage. This is when Clara was[ brought] to live at Faith House.[]

=== Text #5 ===
> Other Minds magazine is a completely free, volunteer based regular publication dedicated to the works of J.R[.]R[.] Tolkien[ by] Tolkien enthusiasts, scholars and those who like to role play in Tolkien's imaginary universe.
This is the first issue of Other Minds Magazine. It has been edited from it's original release under the GFDL[ (]Gnu Free Documentation License[), to] our change to the CC (Creative Commons) license.[][][][][]

=== Text #6 ===
> ﻿Air Weapons and Licensing (Scotland) Bill 2014 Financial Memorandum.
The Scottish Taxi Trade is a large and varied operation, who it[ is] estimated transport more than 1000 million passengers annually. The Scottish Taxi Federation is the only truly representative body of the Scottish Taxi trade.[][]

=== Text #7 ===
> This is a career event for Japanese language teachers!
There will be booths for participating schools, career consultation, special lectures for Japanese language teachers, and many more to cater to a wide range of interests.
For registration and more details, visit IJEC home[ page].[]

=== Text #8 ===
> Ellen Emerson White started writing about Meg Powers in The President's Daughter and continued in White House Autumn, Long Live the Queen, and Long May She Reign, available from Feiwel and Friends (Fall 2007). When she is not writing, she"s watching the Boston Red Sox. She lives in New York City.[][]

=== Text #9 ===
> NASA’s proposed experiments on monkeys were cruel, unnecessary, premature and would have been a[ waste] of[ taxpayers]’ money.
They were expected to cost $1.75 million of US taxpayer money and they are scientifically unsupported. Our video shows that these monkey experiments have been criticized from every side, scientists, animal protectionists, astronauts, former NASA employees, and even the European Space Agency.[][][][][]

=== Text #10 ===
> New tensions threaten to undo all the progress made since 2016 in the talks on the reunification of Cyprus. The row over the exploitation of fossil resources in the Mediterranean has intensified in recent weeks and now the Greek Cypriot President Nicos Anastasiades and the Greek foreign minister have complained about UN Special Adviser Espen Barth Eide. What are the real causes behind the row?[][][][][][][][]

